The concern "search actions" lists hold/unhold/delete in Search.ts. So the fix might involve `deleteMoneyRequestOnSearch` too.

Hmm, maybe the actual fix is in `SearchPageHeader.tsx`: on narrow, when selectionMode enabled but `selectedTransactionsKeys.length === 0`, return null instead of SearchSelectedNarrow. But that wouldn't turn off the bottom tab header.

Actually, the bottom tab header (`HeaderWithBackButton` "Select multiple") is controlled by `selectionMode?.isEnabled`. SearchPageHeader returns SearchSelectedNarrow (the dropdown button) when narrow and selectionMode enabled. Both remain.

Expected: "The select mode will exit because there is no more expense". So both should revert to normal search header.

To exit select mode, must call `turnOffMobileSelectionMode()`. Where? The natural place is `Search` component's effect or `handleDeleteExpenses`.

Let me look at the upstream repo's later code. I might have partial memory: In Expensify App, `Search/index.tsx` currently has:

