```

Still leaves narrow when 0.

Hmm. Wait—maybe the fix is not to turn off on 0 selected, because that would break selection when deselecting. Instead, the fix might be to detect the empty state and turn off. Because after deletion, the selected transactions are cleared AND the data is empty. The condition for exiting select mode is "no more expense", i.e., data empty, not "no selection".

